# scripts/redis/.env — targets for the read-only redis-triage MCP.
#
# Copy to scripts/redis/.env (git-ignored, and blocked by the .env-guard hook) and declare one
# variable per Redis you want to read. Nothing here is a credential — the access gate is your
# cloud IAM / network — but it is per-machine on purpose: a machine with no .env has no targets,
# which is the opt-in.
#
#   REDISPROD_<NAME>=<key>=<value>;<key>=<value>;…      → addressed as target="<name>"
#
# Keys:
#   host    (required)  address of the Redis as seen FROM the tunnel host (or from you, with
#                       tunnel=none) — a private IP or an internal DNS name
#   port                Redis port on that host (default 6379)
#   local   (required)  loopback port this process forwards to. Pick something that is NOT 6379:
#                       6379 is normally your LOCAL dev Redis, and shadowing it would answer a
#                       production question with dev data
#   prod                true (default) ⇒ credential masking + PII provenance for this target
#                       false          ⇒ a staging/test box: values are returned as-is
#   tunnel              gcloud (default) ⇒ this server runs `gcloud compute ssh <vm>
#                                          --zone=<zone> -- -N -L <local>:<host>:<port>`
#                       none             ⇒ already reachable (your own bastion, a VPN, a
#                                          port-forward you manage); nothing is spawned
#   vm, zone            the compute instance to tunnel through (required for tunnel=gcloud)
#
# Examples — replace with your own instances/addresses:

# A staging Redis, tunnelled through a staging VM. prod=false ⇒ values come back unmasked.
# REDISPROD_STAGING=host=10.0.0.10;port=6379;local=6378;prod=false;tunnel=gcloud;vm=staging-vm;zone=your-zone

# The production Redis. prod=true ⇒ credentials are masked at the source and every value is
# fingerprinted into the PII provenance vault.
# REDISPROD_PROD=host=10.0.0.20;port=6379;local=6377;prod=true;tunnel=gcloud;vm=prod-redis-vm;zone=your-zone

# A Redis you can already reach (VPN, bastion, or a forward you run yourself).
# REDISPROD_PROD=host=redis.internal.example.com;port=6379;local=6377;prod=true;tunnel=none
